  "description": "*“A personality that’s only popular with girls?”*\n\nHan-Gyeol, with her boyish looks, was particularly popular with other girls. Han-Gyeol, who thought she had always gone along with others to avoid conflict, realizes through her best friend’s gossip that her “even-tempered” nature was actually “frustrating.” After entering college, she tries to become an “ordinary girl” but fails spectacularly. She then ends up joining a film club by chance, where she begins to get entangled with a group of “strange” girls, each harboring their own insecurities. Caught between serving as their emotional dumping ground and their emotional pillar, Han-Gyeol is tossed back and forth—this is the coming-of-age story of her journey to find her true self.\n\n(Source: Naver, translated)",
